  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social norms and practices by community actors and faith org</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social norms and practices by community actors and faith organisations are shifted towards promoting young women&#x2019;s rights to dignity, bodily integrity and equal participation in decision-making.

IO 3.1 Community actors and Influential faith leaders have created pressure on faith actors to amend existing family laws and procedures. 

OI 3.2 Increased (young) women participation and decision-making in faith organisation (bylaws, governing bodies and internal rules). This includes the appointment of women judges in Shari&#x2019;a Courts and Ecclesiastical Courts. 

OI 3.3 Shari&#x2019;a and Ecclesiastical courts have adopted procedures that facilitate women&#x2019;s access to justice, for example by reducing the procedural fees related to court cases. (Barriers to access to justice). 

[YWCA Palestine input expected on community SBCC and on transforming masculinities with young men and boys]</narrative>
   </description>
